//@version=6
indicator("Adaptive Scanner Engine", "ASR", overlay = true,
     max_labels_count = 100, max_lines_count = 100, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ============================================================================
// ADAPTIVE SCANNER ENGINE  v3.0.0
// Successor to "Adaptive Swing Scanner v1.0".
//
// PHASE 3 — the rules the validation harness selected (see PHASE3_FINDINGS.md).
//   S1  RSI mean reversion: fires on trigger AND trend component >= 18. No
//       regime gate, no score threshold. SWING profile only. Exit: chandelier
//       3xATR from entry, time stop kept, no partial, no fixed target.
//   S2  Donchian breakout: REMOVED. No edge in the trigger (+0.08 R, CI spans 0).
//   S3  EMA momentum: fires on trigger. No score threshold — the score does not
//       predict its outcome; selection among simultaneous S3 candidates is the
//       server's job. Exit: 50% at +1 R, breakeven, chandelier 3xATR on the
//       remainder, NO time stop.
//   S4  Multi-TF trend: unchanged, score >= 75 (the one place the rubric earned
//       its keep). Exit: same as S3.
//   Winner = highest-priority ELIGIBLE strategy, S1 > S4 > S3, by validated
//       expectancy — not the max score. One position per chart at a time.
//   Regime detector: computed and emitted as metadata; no longer a gate.
//   Payload: one alert() per bar carrying an events[] list (ENTRY / SCALE /
//       MODIFY / EXIT / HEARTBEAT) and the full desired_state, so the server
//       reconciles against broker state rather than replaying deltas.
//
//   Profiles shipped:  SWING, POSITIONAL
//   INTRADAY_15M / _5M: evaluated in Phase 5 and NOT shipped. Over 193 RTH
//       sessions x 48 names, ORB, VWAP-reclaim and 15m EMA-cross constructions
//       showed no after-cost edge and none over a random-entry control (which
//       itself loses ~0.1-0.2 R at 5 bps: flat-by-close forgoes the overnight
//       premium). See PHASE5_FINDINGS.md. Building the profile would have been
//       infrastructure ahead of evidence.
//   Entry timing (Phase 6): the signal fires at the daily close; the server
//       fills MARKET-ON-OPEN next session against the absolute stop emitted
//       here. Opening-range and VWAP confirmations on 15m bars lose 0.16-0.17 R
//       per trade to that plain fill on identical signals; pullback limits miss
//       the winners. Nothing intraday gates the entry. See PHASE6_FINDINGS.md.
//   Profiles deferred: LONGTERM (needs S9 fundamentals + S10 monthly overlay)
//   Deliberately NOT shipped: score-driven position sizing. See CONFIDENCE.
//
// WHAT CHANGED FROM v1.0 (every item is a defect fix, not a feature)
//   [F1] Payload reached the server stripped. v1 nested stop/target/scores in
//        objects the TVSignal model does not declare, so they were dropped in
//        transit and orders went out as bare MKT with stop=0. v2 writes the
//        stop into the top-level `stop` field and a structured digest into
//        `comment` — both fields the CURRENT server already accepts — while
//        also emitting the full v2 JSON for the patched server. The bracket
//        now survives an unpatched server.
//   [F2] `confidence` is now emitted. The executor sizes on it; v1 never sent
//        it, so every signal silently took the 1.5%-NAV default and the whole
//        scoring engine had zero effect on capital at risk.
//   [F3] shortEnabled=false no longer suppresses the bar. v1 compared long vs
//        short BEFORE filtering to enabled directions, so a stronger short
//        killed a valid long outright. Direction filtering now precedes argmax.
//   [F4] ATR percentile divided by a hardcoded 252 with no valid-bar guard,
//        understating the percentile during warmup and inflating composite
//        score on short-history symbols. Denominator is now the observed count.
//   [F5] HTF repaint. v1 used request.security(...,"W",expr) with no lookahead,
//        which returns the last CONFIRMED weekly bar in history but the FORMING
//        one in realtime — S1/S4 flipped between backtest and live. Now
//        expr[1] + lookahead_on, which is identical in both.
//   [F6] Warmup gate. Regime needs ~70 bars and the percentiles 252 daily bars.
//        v1 emitted confident-looking output before either was satisfied.
//   [F7] R:R was computed and never enforced. S2's channel-derived stop can
//        produce R:R < 1. Now a hard gate.
//   [F8] Stop/target prices are rounded to syminfo.mintick BEFORE the R:R gate,
//        so the gate tests the price that will actually be worked.
//   [F9] Score comparability. v1 gave S2 a 30-point base for merely triggering
//        (effective floor ~45) while S1 had to earn every point, biasing winner
//        selection toward breakouts. All four are now scored against one
//        five-component rubric and THE TRIGGER IS A BOOLEAN GATE WORTH ZERO.
//  [F10] Day-scale context (SMA200, 52wk range, ADV$, ROC, ATR percentile,
//        12-1 momentum) now comes from a daily request.security context rather
//        than chart-timeframe bar counts, so `roc_20d` means 20 days on every
//        timeframe instead of 77 minutes on a 5m chart.
//  [F11] Fictional position tracking removed. v1 mirrored broker state it could
//        not see and resolved same-bar SL/TP hits ambiguously. The engine now
//        reports only what it last EMITTED, labelled as reference levels.
//  [F12] Hardcoded `hour == 13` gate replaced by a session-relative gate that
//        works on any timeframe and survives bar-alignment changes.
//  [F13] Cooldown is measured in minutes of wall-clock, not bars. The same
//        input meant 75 minutes on 5m and 3 weeks on daily.
//
// STILL UNVALIDATED (Phase 2 blocks on this)
//   The rubric weights below are hand-assigned and have NOT been tested against
//   forward returns. Until the strategy() twin produces an expectancy-by-decile
//   curve per strategy per regime, treat the score as a ranking hint only —
//   which is exactly why useScoreConfidence defaults to OFF.
//
// DEPLOYMENT
//   Alert condition: "Any alert() function call"
//   Webhook URL:     https://<host>/webhook?token=<TV_WEBHOOK_TOKEN>
//   Message:         leave empty — alert() supplies the payload
//   NOTE: TradingView snapshots the script at alert-creation time. Any edit to
//   this file requires re-creating every alert. The server should reject any
//   payload whose schema_version is below its floor so stale alerts surface.
// ============================================================================


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                              PROFILE                                     ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
enum Profile
    SWING      = "SWING — 4H/1D, days to weeks"
    POSITIONAL = "POSITIONAL — 1D/1W, weeks to months"

profile     = input.enum(Profile.SWING, "Profile", group = "Profile",
     tooltip = "Selects the parameter set. INTRADAY and LONGTERM profiles ship in Phase 5 / Phase 3 respectively — they need sub-strategies that do not exist yet, and shipping them as parameter tweaks of the swing engine would be dishonest.")
isSwing     = profile == Profile.SWING
profileStr  = isSwing ? "SWING" : "POSITIONAL"

// Profile-resolved defaults. Operator overrides live in the groups below.
p_cooldownMin   = isSwing ?  7200 : 21600     // 5 days vs 15 trading days
p_minRR         = 1.5                          // guards degenerate geometry only; S3/S4 designed ratios are 1.6-1.7
p_atrStopMult   = isSwing ?   1.5 :   2.75
p_timeStopDays  = isSwing ?    15 :    60      // S1 only in v3; S3/S4 have no time stop
p_s1Enabled     = isSwing                      // S1 with wide POSITIONAL stops loses (+0.10 R, 32% hit); SWING only
// S3 gating is profile-dependent: the score is not a predictor anywhere, but
// under a portfolio slot cap it acts as a RATE LIMITER, and in POSITIONAL the
// unthrottled S3 stream crowds out S4's longer, better trades. Resolved by the
// slot-capped simulation in PHASE3_FINDINGS.md.
p_s3Enabled     = isSwing or s3_inPositional
p_s3EmitAll     = s3_gate <= 0.0
s3_minScoreGate = s3_gate


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                           MASTER CONTROLS                                ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
s4_minScore     = input.float(75.0, "S4 min score (validated 70-75; degrades above 80)",
     minval = 0.0, maxval = 95.0, step = 1.0, group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "The only strategy whose score predicts outcome. Phase 2 sweep: >=60 +0.175 R, >=70 +0.193, >=75 +0.211, >=80 +0.157.")
s1_trendGate    = input.float(18.0, "S1 trend-component gate (>= means above SMA200)",
     minval = 0.0, maxval = 25.0, step = 1.0, group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "S1 fires on trigger AND its own trend component >= this. 18 = above SMA200; 25 = SMA50 > SMA200 too. Replaces the regime gate that discarded 99.8% of S1's edge.")
s3_gate         = input.float(70.0, "S3 score gate (rate limiter, not a predictor)",
     minval = 0.0, maxval = 95.0, step = 1.0, group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "The S3 score does not predict its outcome (Spearman +0.015), but under a portfolio slot cap the unthrottled S3 stream crowds out S4. At cap 10 the gate raised SWING Sharpe from 0.83 to 1.03. Set 0 only if you run more than ~20 concurrent slots.")
s3_inPositional = input.bool(false, "Enable S3 in POSITIONAL (validated OFF)", group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "POSITIONAL is S4-only by evidence: at cap 10, S4-only Sharpe 1.27 / max DD -11 R vs 1.03 / -20 R with S3. Turning S3 on buys capacity at the cost of Sharpe and drawdown.")
shortEnabled    = input.bool(false, "Compute short scores (metadata only; never deployed)", group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "Every strategy's short trigger tested negative. Short scores are still computed for the payload; selection is long-only.")
useRegimeFilter = input.bool(false, "Enforce Regime-Strategy Alignment (validated OFF)", group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "As a gate this blocked 84% of S1 triggers and added +0.01 R to S3. Regime is still computed and emitted as metadata.")
cooldownMin     = input.int(0, "Cooldown (minutes, 0 = profile default)", minval = 0,
     group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "Wall-clock, not bars. v1 used bars, which meant 75 minutes on a 5m chart and three weeks on a daily chart from the same input.")
minRR           = input.float(0.0, "Minimum R:R to fire (0 = profile default)",
     minval = 0.0, maxval = 6.0, step = 0.1, group = "Master Controls",
     tooltip = "v1 computed rrRatio and never enforced it. S2's channel-derived stop can produce R:R below 1.")

effCooldown  = cooldownMin > 0   ? cooldownMin : p_cooldownMin
effMinRR     = minRR       > 0.0 ? minRR       : p_minRR

// ── Session gating (replaces the hardcoded 13:00 NY check) ──────────────────
useSessionGate = input.bool(true, "Restrict firing to a session window", group = "Session Gate",
     tooltip = "v1 hardcoded `hour == 13`, valid only for 4H US-equity charts. On a 5m chart it fired exactly once a day at 13:00. Turn OFF for futures, FX, or 1D+ charts where every confirmed close is actionable.")
gateSession    = input.session("0930-1600", "Tradeable session (exchange time)", group = "Session Gate")
fireOnLastBar  = input.bool(false, "Fire only on the session's last bar", group = "Session Gate",
     tooltip = "For end-of-day decision making on intraday charts. Ignored on 1D and higher.")
noEntryAfter   = input.int(0, "Block entries after this hour (exchange time, 0 = off)",
     minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Session Gate")

// ── Confidence → position size ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// The executor sizes on `confidence`: >=0.8 -> 2.0% NAV, 0.6-0.8 -> 1.5%,
// <0.6 -> 1.0%, and rejects below 0.3. v1 emitted no confidence at all, so
// every signal took the unset default of 1.5%.
//
// Phase 1 deliberately restores that 1.5% behaviour EXACTLY (constant 0.6)
// rather than letting an unvalidated score drive real position size. Turn
// useScoreConfidence ON only after Phase 2 shows expectancy is monotone in
// score. That is the whole point of the sequencing.
useScoreConfidence = input.bool(false, "Derive confidence from score (REQUIRES Phase 2 validation)",
     group = "Confidence",
     tooltip = "OFF = emit a constant 0.6, reproducing today's flat 1.5%-NAV sizing. ON = map score linearly onto the confidence band, which makes an unvalidated rubric decide how much money is at risk. Do not turn this on before the expectancy-by-decile curve exists.")
confFlat     = input.float(0.60, "Flat confidence when derivation is OFF",
     minval = 0.31, maxval = 0.99, step = 0.01, group = "Confidence")
confAtMin    = input.float(0.45, "Confidence at min score", minval = 0.30, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.01, group = "Confidence")
confAtMax    = input.float(0.95, "Confidence at score 100", minval = 0.35, maxval = 1.00, step = 0.01, group = "Confidence")

// ── Display ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
showRegimeBG   = input.bool(false, "Regime background", group = "Display")
showStratLabel = input.bool(false, "Strategy name on signals", group = "Display")
showLevels     = input.bool(true,  "Reference SL/TP lines for last emitted signal", group = "Display")
showDash       = input.bool(true,  "Dashboard", group = "Display")


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                        INDICATOR PARAMETERS                              ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// These are CHART-TIMEFRAME lengths and are meant to be. ADX(14) on a 4H chart
// is a legitimate 4H trend measure. What must NOT be chart-timeframe is the
// day-scale context (SMA200, 52wk range, ADV$, ROC-in-days, ATR percentile);
// that now comes from the daily context block below. See [F10].
adxLen      = input.int(14, "ADX Length",        minval = 7,  maxval = 30, group = "Regime Detection")
adxTrendThr = input.int(25, "ADX Trending",      minval = 15, maxval = 40, group = "Regime Detection")
adxRangeThr = input.int(20, "ADX Range-Bound",   minval = 10, maxval = 25, group = "Regime Detection")
chopLen     = input.int(14, "Choppiness Length", minval = 5,  maxval = 30, group = "Regime Detection")
bbwLen      = input.int(20, "BB Width Length",   minval = 10, maxval = 50, group = "Regime Detection")
bbwStd      = input.float(2.0, "BB Width StdDev", minval = 1.0, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.5, group = "Regime Detection")

s1_rsiLen     = input.int(14, "S1: RSI Length",      minval = 2,  maxval = 50, group = "S1 Mean Reversion")
s1_oversold   = input.int(30, "S1: Oversold",        minval = 10, maxval = 45, group = "S1 Mean Reversion")
s1_overbought = input.int(70, "S1: Overbought",      minval = 55, maxval = 90, group = "S1 Mean Reversion")
s1_supportLen = input.int(20, "S1: Support Lookback", minval = 5, maxval = 60, group = "S1 Mean Reversion")

s3_fastEMA  = input.int(9,  "S3: Fast EMA",  minval = 3,  maxval = 30,  group = "S3 EMA/VWAP Momentum")
s3_slowEMA  = input.int(21, "S3: Slow EMA",  minval = 10, maxval = 50,  group = "S3 EMA/VWAP Momentum")
s3_trendEMA = input.int(50, "S3: Trend EMA", minval = 30, maxval = 200, group = "S3 EMA/VWAP Momentum")
s3_macdFast = input.int(12, "S3: MACD Fast",   minval = 5,  maxval = 20, group = "S3 EMA/VWAP Momentum")
s3_macdSlow = input.int(26, "S3: MACD Slow",   minval = 15, maxval = 40, group = "S3 EMA/VWAP Momentum")
s3_macdSig  = input.int(9,  "S3: MACD Signal", minval = 3,  maxval = 15, group = "S3 EMA/VWAP Momentum")
s3_crossMax = input.int(5,  "S3: Max bars since cross", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = "S3 EMA/VWAP Momentum")

s4_wkFast   = input.int(20, "S4: Weekly Fast EMA", minval = 5,  maxval = 50,  group = "S4 Multi-TF Trend")
s4_wkSlow   = input.int(50, "S4: Weekly Slow EMA", minval = 20, maxval = 100, group = "S4 Multi-TF Trend")
s4_dailyEMA = input.int(21, "S4: Entry EMA",       minval = 5,  maxval = 50,  group = "S4 Multi-TF Trend")
s4_rsiPBLo  = input.int(40, "S4: Pullback Buy Zone",  minval = 25, maxval = 50, group = "S4 Multi-TF Trend")
s4_rsiPBHi  = input.int(60, "S4: Pullback Sell Zone", minval = 50, maxval = 75, group = "S4 Multi-TF Trend")

atrLen       = input.int(14, "ATR Length (chart TF)", minval = 5, maxval = 30, group = "Risk")
atrStopMult  = input.float(0.0, "ATR Stop Multiple (0 = profile default)",
     minval = 0.0, maxval = 6.0, step = 0.25, group = "Risk")
minDollarVol = input.float(5.0, "Min 20-DAY Avg Dollar Volume ($M)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 500.0, step = 1.0,
     group = "Risk",
     tooltip = "Twenty DAYS, sourced from the daily context — not twenty chart bars. v1 used volSMA20*close on the chart timeframe, which on a 5m chart measured 100 minutes of volume.")
minPrice     = input.float(5.0, "Min Price", minval = 0.0, step = 0.5, group = "Risk")

effAtrStop = atrStopMult > 0.0 ? atrStopMult : p_atrStopMult


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                    TIMEFRAME NORMALIZATION LAYER                         ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// Every quantity expressed in DAYS must resolve to the same thing on 5m, 15m,
// 4H, 1D and 1W. Two mechanisms:
//   1. bpd (bars per trading day) converts day-counts into chart bars for the
//      few chart-timeframe things that are genuinely day-scaled (time stops).
//   2. The daily context block supplies everything with a lookback beyond
//      ~60 trading days, because those are either meaningless or literally
//      uncomputable on the chart timeframe. 252 daily bars at 5m would need
//      19,656 bars of history, past Pine's 5,000-bar ceiling.
sessionSec = input.int(23400, "Trading seconds per session", minval = 3600, maxval = 86400,
     group = "Timeframe Normalization",
     tooltip = "23400 = 6.5h US equity RTH. 57600 for extended hours. ~82800 for most futures. Used to convert day-counts into chart bars.")

tfSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
bpd   = timeframe.isintraday ? math.max(1.0, math.round(sessionSec / math.max(1.0, tfSec))) :
        timeframe.isdaily    ? 1.0 :
        timeframe.isweekly   ? 0.2 :
        timeframe.ismonthly  ? 1.0 / 21.0 : 1.0

// Diagnostic: count bars actually observed per session and compare to the
// formula. A large divergence means sessionSec is wrong for this instrument
// (half-days, extended hours toggled, non-US session) and every day-scaled
// quantity is off. Emitted in the payload rather than silently absorbed.
var int   barsThisSess = 0
var float bpdObs       = na
var int   sessSeen     = 0
if timeframe.isintraday
    barsThisSess += 1
    if session.islastbar and barstate.isconfirmed
        bpdObs       := na(bpdObs) ? barsThisSess : bpdObs + 0.2 * (barsThisSess - bpdObs)
        sessSeen     += 1
        barsThisSess := 0
bpdDrift = timeframe.isintraday and sessSeen >= 5 and not na(bpdObs) ? math.abs(bpdObs - bpd) / bpd * 100.0 : 0.0

// Used by the Phase 5 intraday profile to express time stops and opening-range
// windows in days/minutes rather than bars. Kept here so the normalization
// layer has one owner.
barsForDays(float days) => math.max(1, int(math.round(days * bpd)))


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                          DAILY CONTEXT  [F10]                            ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// One tuple-returning request.security call carries every day-scale feature.
// Tuple returns count as a single call against the 40-per-script budget.
//
// bpy = bars per year on whichever timeframe the context is computed. On an
// intraday chart the context is pulled from "D" so bpy = 252. On a 1D+ chart
// we compute it locally on the chart timeframe (requesting a LOWER timeframe
// than the chart with lookahead_on would be genuine forward-looking bias), so
// bpy scales to 252 / 52 / 12.
// On an intraday chart the context is pulled from "D". On 1D and above it is
// pulled from the chart's own timeframe, because requesting a LOWER timeframe
// than the chart with lookahead_on is genuine forward-looking bias. Either way
// the context is the last CONFIRMED bar of ctxTf, so on a 1D chart the context
// is as of yesterday's close. That lag is deliberate: it is what makes the
// values identical in backtest and in realtime.
ctxFromDaily = tfSec < 86400
ctxBpy       = ctxFromDaily        ? 252 :
               timeframe.isweekly  ? 52  :
               timeframe.ismonthly ? 12  : 252

f_ctx(simple int bpy) =>
    nAtr = math.max(2, int(math.round(bpy / 18.0)))    // ~14 days
    nAdv = math.max(2, int(math.round(bpy / 12.6)))    // ~20 days
    n50  = math.max(2, int(math.round(bpy / 5.04)))    // ~50 days
    n200 = math.max(2, int(math.round(bpy / 1.26)))    // ~200 days
    n1m  = math.max(1, int(math.round(bpy / 12.6)))    // ~20 days
    n3m  = math.max(1, int(math.round(bpy / 4.2)))     // ~60 days
    n6m  = math.max(1, int(math.round(bpy / 2.0)))     // ~126 days
    n12m = math.max(2, bpy)

    _atr  = ta.atr(nAtr)
    _rsi  = ta.rsi(close, 14)
    [_dp, _dm, _adx] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
    _s50  = ta.sma(close, n50)
    _s200 = ta.sma(close, n200)
    _adv  = ta.sma(volume, nAdv) * close
    _hi   = ta.highest(high, n12m)
    _lo   = ta.lowest(low,  n12m)
    _r1   = close[n1m] > 0 ? (close - close[n1m]) / close[n1m] * 100.0 : na
    _r2   = close[n3m] > 0 ? (close - close[n3m]) / close[n3m] * 100.0 : na
    _r3   = close[n6m] > 0 ? (close - close[n6m]) / close[n6m] * 100.0 : na
    // 12-1 momentum: twelve-month return excluding the most recent month, the
    // standard construction that strips short-term reversal.
    _m121 = close[n12m] > 0 and not na(close[n1m]) ? (close[n1m] / close[n12m] - 1.0) * 100.0 : na

    // [F4] ATR percentile against the number of bars ACTUALLY observed, not a
    // hardcoded 252. v1's fixed denominator understated the percentile during
    // warmup and on short-history symbols, which inflated composite score via
    // the (100 - atrPctile) term and pushed new listings to the top of the rank.
    _atrPrev = _atr[1]
    _seen = 0
    _cnt  = 0
    for i = 2 to n12m + 1
        if not na(_atr[i]) and not na(_atrPrev)
            _seen += 1
            if _atrPrev > _atr[i]
                _cnt += 1
    _atrP = _seen >= 20 ? _cnt / _seen * 100.0 : na

    _gap  = close[1] > 0 ? (open - close[1]) / close[1] * 100.0 : na
    _abs  = math.abs(nz(_gap))
    _gapA = ta.sma(_abs, nAdv)

    // [F5] Every element is returned at offset [1] so that, combined with
    // lookahead_on at the call site, the value is the last CONFIRMED higher-
    // timeframe bar — identical in history and in realtime. v1 used neither,
    // which is why S1/S4 flipped between backtest and live.
    [_atr[1], _atrP, _adv[1], _hi[1], _lo[1], _r1[1], _r2[1], _r3[1], _m121[1],
     _s50[1], _s200[1], _rsi[1], _adx[1], _gapA[1], bar_index[1]]

ctxTf = ctxFromDaily ? "D" : timeframe.period
[dAtr, dAtrPct, dAdvUsd, dHi52, dLo52, dRoc20, dRoc60, dRoc126, dMom121,
 dSma50, dSma200, dRsi, dAdx, dGapAvg, dCtxBars] =
     request.security(syminfo.tickerid, ctxTf, f_ctx(ctxBpy), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

dRange52   = nz(dHi52) - nz(dLo52)
distFromHi = dRange52 > 0 ? (dHi52 - close) / dRange52 * 100.0 : na   // 0 = at high
distFromLo = dRange52 > 0 ? (close - dLo52) / dRange52 * 100.0 : na   // 0 = at low


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                       CHART-TIMEFRAME CALCULATIONS                       ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
atr      = ta.atr(atrLen)
[diPlus, diMinus, adxVal] = ta.dmi(adxLen, adxLen)
rsi14    = ta.rsi(close, 14)
volSMA20 = ta.sma(volume, 20)
relVol   = volSMA20 > 0 ? volume / volSMA20 : na

// Relative-volume percentile over 50 chart bars, valid-bar guarded.
// NOTE: this is NOT time-of-day normalized. On an intraday chart it compares a
// 10:05 bar against a 14:30 bar, which is meaningless — intraday volume has a
// strong U-shaped seasonality. The Phase 5 intraday profile replaces this with
// a per-minute-of-day EWMA. Until then, treat rvPctile as daily-and-slower.
rvSeen = 0
rvCnt  = 0
for i = 1 to 50
    if not na(volSMA20[i]) and volSMA20[i] > 0 and not na(relVol)
        rvSeen += 1
        if relVol > (volume[i] / volSMA20[i])
            rvCnt += 1
rvPctile = rvSeen >= 20 ? rvCnt / rvSeen * 100.0 : na

volAboveAvg = not na(volSMA20) and volume > volSMA20 * 1.15


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                          REGIME DETECTION                                ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
chopATR = math.sum(ta.tr, chopLen)
chopHL  = ta.highest(high, chopLen) - ta.lowest(low, chopLen)
chop    = chopHL > 0 ? 100.0 * math.log10(chopATR / chopHL) / math.log10(chopLen) : na

[bbMid, bbUp, bbLo] = ta.bb(close, bbwLen, bbwStd)
bbw            = bbMid != 0 ? (bbUp - bbLo) / bbMid * 100.0 : na
bbwSMA         = ta.sma(bbw, 50)
bbwExpanding   = not na(bbwSMA) and bbw > bbwSMA * 1.1
bbwContracting = not na(bbwSMA) and bbw < bbwSMA * 0.9

atrSMA50     = ta.sma(atr, 50)
atrExpanding = not na(atrSMA50) and atr > atrSMA50 * 1.2

cChop = nz(chop, 50.0)
trendScore    = math.min((adxVal > adxTrendThr ? (adxVal - adxTrendThr) / 15.0 : 0.0) +
     (cChop < 38.2 ? (38.2 - cChop) / 20.0 : 0.0), 1.0) * 100.0
breakoutScore = math.min((atrExpanding ? 0.4 : 0.0) + (bbwExpanding ? 0.4 : 0.0) +
     (adxVal > adxRangeThr ? 0.2 : 0.0), 1.0) * 100.0
meanRevScore  = math.min((adxVal < adxRangeThr ? (adxRangeThr - adxVal) / 10.0 : 0.0) +
     (cChop > 61.8 ? (cChop - 61.8) / 20.0 : 0.0) + (bbwContracting ? 0.3 : 0.0), 1.0) * 100.0
momentumScore = math.min((adxVal > adxRangeThr and adxVal <= adxTrendThr ? 0.5 : 0.0) +
     (not bbwContracting and not bbwExpanding ? 0.3 : 0.0) +
     (math.abs(nz(dRoc20)) > 3.0 ? 0.2 : 0.0), 1.0) * 100.0

regimeTrend    = trendScore    >= 60
regimeBreakout = breakoutScore >= 60
regimeMeanRev  = meanRevScore  >= 60
regimeMomentum = momentumScore >= 55 and not regimeBreakout and not regimeTrend and not regimeMeanRev

regime    = regimeBreakout ? 2 : regimeTrend ? 4 : regimeMomentum ? 3 : regimeMeanRev ? 1 : 0
regimeStr = regime == 1 ? "MEAN_REV" : regime == 2 ? "BREAKOUT" : regime == 3 ? "MOMENTUM" :
            regime == 4 ? "TRENDING" : "NEUTRAL"
regimeConf = regime == 1 ? meanRevScore : regime == 2 ? breakoutScore :
             regime == 3 ? momentumScore : regime == 4 ? trendScore : 0.0

// Secondary regime by rank rather than float equality. v1 compared computed
// float sums with == to identify the runner-up, which is fragile and could
// mislabel it.
r2Score = 0.0
r2Id    = 0
if regime != 1 and meanRevScore > r2Score
    r2Score := meanRevScore
    r2Id    := 1
if regime != 2 and breakoutScore > r2Score
    r2Score := breakoutScore
    r2Id    := 2
if regime != 3 and momentumScore > r2Score
    r2Score := momentumScore
    r2Id    := 3
if regime != 4 and trendScore > r2Score
    r2Score := trendScore
    r2Id    := 4
regime2Str = r2Id == 1 ? "MEAN_REV" : r2Id == 2 ? "BREAKOUT" : r2Id == 3 ? "MOMENTUM" :
             r2Id == 4 ? "TRENDING" : "NEUTRAL"


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                     SUB-STRATEGY SCORING  [F9]                           ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// One rubric for all four, and THE TRIGGER IS A BOOLEAN GATE WORTH ZERO POINTS.
//
// v1 gave S2 a flat 30 points for merely breaking the channel, plus 10 for any
// volume and 5 for any regime — an effective floor of 45 before it demonstrated
// anything — while S1 had to earn every one of its points. Comparing those two
// numbers to pick a winner, and then ranking them cross-sectionally against
// other symbols, was comparing different units. The rubric below is the same
// 100 points spent the same way in all four strategies:
//
//   trend alignment      0-25   is the higher-timeframe backdrop with us
//   momentum quality     0-25   is the move itself any good
//   volatility/location  0-20   is this a sane place to be entering
//   volume confirmation  0-15   did participation confirm it
//   HTF / regime context 0-15   does the prevailing regime favour this style
//
// The scores are STILL hand-assigned and still unvalidated. What has changed is
// that they are now comparable to each other, which is a precondition for the
// Phase 2 expectancy-by-decile work, not a substitute for it.
f_rubric(bool trig, float trend, float mom, float loc, float vol, float htf) =>
    trig ? math.min(100.0, math.max(0.0, trend) + math.max(0.0, mom) +
           math.max(0.0, loc) + math.max(0.0, vol) + math.max(0.0, htf)) : 0.0

// Shared building blocks
aboveLT   = not na(dSma200) and close > dSma200
belowLT   = not na(dSma200) and close < dSma200
ltUp      = not na(dSma50) and not na(dSma200) and dSma50 > dSma200
ltDn      = not na(dSma50) and not na(dSma200) and dSma50 < dSma200
volScore  = (volAboveAvg ? 10.0 : 0.0) + (nz(rvPctile, 50.0) > 70.0 ? 5.0 : 0.0)
atrSane   = not na(dAtrPct) and dAtrPct >= 15.0 and dAtrPct <= 85.0

// ── S1: RSI Mean Reversion ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
s1_rsi        = ta.rsi(close, s1_rsiLen)
s1_nearSupp   = close - ta.lowest(low, s1_supportLen) < atr * 1.5
s1_nearResist = ta.highest(high, s1_supportLen) - close < atr * 1.5
s1_trigL      = s1_rsi < s1_oversold   and s1_nearSupp
s1_trigS      = s1_rsi > s1_overbought and s1_nearResist

s1_trendC    = aboveLT and ltUp ? 25.0 : aboveLT ? 18.0 : not na(dSma50) and close > dSma50 ? 10.0 : 0.0
s1_scoreLong = f_rubric(s1_trigL,
     s1_trendC,
     (s1_rsi < s1_oversold - 10 ? 25.0 : s1_rsi < s1_oversold - 5 ? 20.0 : 14.0),
     (nz(distFromHi, 50.0) > 50.0 ? 12.0 : nz(distFromHi, 50.0) > 30.0 ? 7.0 : 3.0) + (atrSane ? 8.0 : 0.0),
     volScore,
     (regimeMeanRev ? 15.0 : regime == 0 ? 8.0 : 0.0))

s1_scoreShort = f_rubric(s1_trigS,
     (belowLT and ltDn ? 25.0 : belowLT ? 18.0 : not na(dSma50) and close < dSma50 ? 10.0 : 0.0),
     (s1_rsi > s1_overbought + 10 ? 25.0 : s1_rsi > s1_overbought + 5 ? 20.0 : 14.0),
     (nz(distFromLo, 50.0) > 50.0 ? 12.0 : nz(distFromLo, 50.0) > 30.0 ? 7.0 : 3.0) + (atrSane ? 8.0 : 0.0),
     volScore,
     (regimeMeanRev ? 15.0 : regime == 0 ? 8.0 : 0.0))

// ── S3: EMA / VWAP Momentum ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
s3_fast  = ta.ema(close, s3_fastEMA)
s3_slow  = ta.ema(close, s3_slowEMA)
s3_trend = ta.ema(close, s3_trendEMA)
[s3_macd, s3_sig, s3_hist] = ta.macd(close, s3_macdFast, s3_macdSlow, s3_macdSig)
// VWAP is only meaningful intraday; on daily and above use a volume-weighted MA.
s3_anchor = timeframe.isintraday ? ta.vwap(hlc3) : ta.vwma(close, 20)
s3_bsUp   = ta.barssince(ta.crossover(s3_fast, s3_slow))
s3_bsDn   = ta.barssince(ta.crossunder(s3_fast, s3_slow))
// Require a RECENT cross so we score an event, not a persistent state.
s3_trigL  = not na(s3_bsUp) and s3_bsUp <= s3_crossMax and rsi14 <= 70
s3_trigS  = not na(s3_bsDn) and s3_bsDn <= s3_crossMax and rsi14 >= 30

s3_scoreLong = f_rubric(s3_trigL,
     (close > s3_trend ? 12.0 : 0.0) + (close > s3_anchor ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (aboveLT ? 5.0 : 0.0),
     (s3_hist > 0 and rsi14 > 50 ? 15.0 : s3_hist > 0 ? 8.0 : 0.0) +
     (nz(dRoc20) > 3.0 ? 6.0 : 0.0) + (s3_hist > nz(s3_hist[1]) ? 4.0 : 0.0),
     (s3_fast > s3_slow ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (close - s3_trend < atr * 3.0 ? 6.0 : 0.0) + (atrSane ? 6.0 : 0.0),
     volScore,
     (regimeMomentum ? 15.0 : regime == 4 ? 10.0 : regime == 2 ? 8.0 : regime == 0 ? 5.0 : 0.0))

s3_scoreShort = f_rubric(s3_trigS,
     (close < s3_trend ? 12.0 : 0.0) + (close < s3_anchor ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (belowLT ? 5.0 : 0.0),
     (s3_hist < 0 and rsi14 < 50 ? 15.0 : s3_hist < 0 ? 8.0 : 0.0) +
     (nz(dRoc20) < -3.0 ? 6.0 : 0.0) + (s3_hist < nz(s3_hist[1]) ? 4.0 : 0.0),
     (s3_fast < s3_slow ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (s3_trend - close < atr * 3.0 ? 6.0 : 0.0) + (atrSane ? 6.0 : 0.0),
     volScore,
     (regimeMomentum ? 15.0 : regime == 4 ? 10.0 : regime == 2 ? 8.0 : regime == 0 ? 5.0 : 0.0))

// ── S4: Multi-Timeframe Trend ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// [F5] Weekly context at offset [1] with lookahead_on: last CONFIRMED weekly
// bar, identical in history and realtime. v1 used neither and repainted.
f_wk() =>
    _f = ta.ema(close, s4_wkFast)
    _s = ta.ema(close, s4_wkSlow)
    [_dp, _dm, _a] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
    [_f[1], _s[1], close[1], _a[1]]

wkTf = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) < timeframe.in_seconds("W") ? "W" : timeframe.period
[s4_wkF, s4_wkS, s4_wkC, s4_wkADX] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, wkTf, f_wk(),
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

s4_dEMA  = ta.ema(close, s4_dailyEMA)
[s4_macd, s4_sig, s4_h] = ta.macd(close, 12, 26, 9)
s4_wkBull = not na(s4_wkF) and not na(s4_wkS) and s4_wkF > s4_wkS and s4_wkC > s4_wkF
s4_wkBear = not na(s4_wkF) and not na(s4_wkS) and s4_wkF < s4_wkS and s4_wkC < s4_wkF
s4_pbBuy  = rsi14 < s4_rsiPBLo and rsi14 > 25
s4_pbSell = rsi14 > s4_rsiPBHi and rsi14 < 75
s4_bounce = close > s4_dEMA and close[1] <= s4_dEMA[1]
s4_reject = close < s4_dEMA and close[1] >= s4_dEMA[1]
s4_trigL  = s4_wkBull and (s4_pbBuy  or s4_bounce)
s4_trigS  = s4_wkBear and (s4_pbSell or s4_reject)

s4_scoreLong = f_rubric(s4_trigL,
     (s4_wkBull ? 15.0 : 0.0) + (aboveLT ? 10.0 : 0.0),
     (nz(s4_wkADX) > 20.0 ? 10.0 : 0.0) + (s4_macd > s4_sig ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (nz(dMom121) > 0.0 ? 7.0 : 0.0),
     (s4_pbBuy ? 12.0 : s4_bounce ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (atrSane ? 8.0 : 0.0),
     volScore,
     (regimeTrend ? 15.0 : regime == 3 ? 10.0 : regime == 0 ? 5.0 : 0.0))

s4_scoreShort = f_rubric(s4_trigS,
     (s4_wkBear ? 15.0 : 0.0) + (belowLT ? 10.0 : 0.0),
     (nz(s4_wkADX) > 20.0 ? 10.0 : 0.0) + (s4_macd < s4_sig ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (nz(dMom121) < 0.0 ? 7.0 : 0.0),
     (s4_pbSell ? 12.0 : s4_reject ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (atrSane ? 8.0 : 0.0),
     volScore,
     (regimeTrend ? 15.0 : regime == 3 ? 10.0 : regime == 0 ? 5.0 : 0.0))


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║              WINNER SELECTION — priority by validated expectancy          ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// v2 took the max score across strategies. Phase 2 showed the scores are not
// comparable predictors (S3's is noise, S1's is noise, S4's is weak), so the
// argmax was choosing on decoration. Each strategy now has its OWN validated
// gate, and the winner is the highest-priority eligible one — priority being
// the order of measured expectancy: S1 (+0.47 R) > S4 (+0.21) > S3 (+0.15).
// Long-only: every short trigger tested negative. Short scores remain
// computed for the payload.
s1_aligned = not useRegimeFilter or regime == 1 or regime == 0
s3_aligned = not useRegimeFilter or regime == 3 or regime == 4 or regime == 0
s4_aligned = not useRegimeFilter or regime == 4 or regime == 0

s1L = s1_aligned ? s1_scoreLong : 0.0
s3L = s3_aligned ? s3_scoreLong : 0.0
s4L = s4_aligned ? s4_scoreLong : 0.0
s1S = shortEnabled and s1_aligned ? s1_scoreShort : 0.0
s3S = shortEnabled and s3_aligned ? s3_scoreShort : 0.0
s4S = shortEnabled and s4_aligned ? s4_scoreShort : 0.0

s1_elig = p_s1Enabled and s1_aligned and s1_trigL and s1_trendC >= s1_trendGate
s3_elig = p_s3Enabled and s3_aligned and s3_trigL and (p_s3EmitAll or s3_scoreLong >= s3_minScoreGate)
s4_elig = s4_aligned and s4_trigL and s4_scoreLong >= s4_minScore

bestStrat = s1_elig ? 1 : s4_elig ? 4 : s3_elig ? 3 : 0
bestScore = bestStrat == 1 ? s1_scoreLong : bestStrat == 4 ? s4_scoreLong : bestStrat == 3 ? s3_scoreLong : 0.0
isLong    = true
bestDir   = "BUY"

stratName(int id) => id == 1 ? "RSI_MeanReversion" : id == 3 ? "EMA_VWAP_Momentum" : id == 4 ? "MultiTF_Trend" : "None"
stratTag(int id)  => id == 1 ? "MR" : id == 3 ? "MOM" : id == 4 ? "MTF" : "--"


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                        RISK LEVELS  [F7] [F8]                            ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// Stops are ATR multiples scaled by the profile; targets are STRUCTURAL where a
// structure exists. That matters: if the target were simply stop * targetRR the
// R:R gate would be circular and would pass by construction.
//
// The designed geometries are S1 1.2/~2.5, S2 channel-based, S3 1.8/3.0,
// S4 2.5/4.0 — R:R of roughly 2.1, 1.67 and 1.6. The gate default is 1.5: it
// catches degenerate geometry only and never vetoes a designed ratio (a 2.0
// gate in the first draft left SPY with one signal in twelve years). The
// target scales with the profile alongside the stop.
//
// In v3 the fixed target is only the INITIAL bracket. The exit engine below
// replaces it: S1 trails a 3xATR chandelier from entry with the profile time
// stop; S3/S4 take 50% at +1 R, move to breakeven, and trail the remainder
// with no time stop. `tpPrice` remains in the payload as the partial level
// (S3/S4) or the reference target (S1).
stopScale = effAtrStop / 1.5
tpScale   = stopScale

s1_stopD = atr * 1.20 * stopScale
s3_stopD = atr * 1.80 * stopScale
s4_stopD = atr * 2.50 * stopScale
stopDist = bestStrat == 1 ? s1_stopD : bestStrat == 3 ? s3_stopD : s4_stopD

// Reference targets (S1: band mid / prior extreme; S3, S4: ATR projections).
// For S3/S4 the deployed partial level is +1 R, computed in the exit engine.
s1_tpD = math.min(math.max(math.abs(nz(bbMid, close) - close), atr * 1.5 * tpScale), atr * 4.0 * tpScale)
s3_tpD = atr * 3.0 * tpScale
s4_tpD = atr * 4.0 * tpScale
tpDist = bestStrat == 1 ? s1_tpD : bestStrat == 3 ? s3_tpD : s4_tpD

// [F8] Round to mintick BEFORE measuring R:R, so the gate tests the price that
// will actually be worked at the broker. v1 emitted unrounded prices, which
// IBKR can reject outright.
entryRef  = math.round_to_mintick(close)
stopPrice = math.round_to_mintick(isLong ? close - stopDist : close + stopDist)
tpPrice   = math.round_to_mintick(isLong ? close + tpDist   : close - tpDist)
realRisk  = math.abs(entryRef - stopPrice)
realRwd   = math.abs(tpPrice  - entryRef)
rrRatio   = realRisk > 0 ? realRwd / realRisk : 0.0
rrOk      = rrRatio >= effMinRR                      // [F7] now enforced
stopPct   = close > 0 ? realRisk / close * 100.0 : 0.0


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                     EXIT ENGINE — state                                  ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// The one place the indicator carries state: the position it last ENTERED,
// managed bar by bar with the same fill rules as the validation labeller
// (research/labels.py: label_event_v3). This is not a claim about broker
// state — the server reconciles `desired_state` against IBKR — it is the
// engine's declaration of what the position should look like now.
//
// Exit models selected in the Phase 3 study (train 2015-20, confirmed 2021+):
//   S1      chandelier k*ATR from entry, no partial, profile time stop kept
//   S3, S4  50% off at +1 R, stop to breakeven, chandelier k*ATR on the
//           remainder, no fixed target, NO time stop
exit_trailK     = input.float(3.0, "Chandelier trail (x ATR)", minval = 1.0, maxval = 6.0, step = 0.5, group = "Exit Engine",
     tooltip = "3.0 selected on train Sharpe; 2.0 exits too early on every strategy, 4.0 collapses out of sample for S1.")
exit_partialR   = input.float(1.0, "S3/S4 partial at (R)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.25, group = "Exit Engine")
exit_partialPct = input.int(50, "S3/S4 partial size (%)", minval = 10, maxval = 90, step = 10, group = "Exit Engine")
emitHeartbeat   = input.bool(true, "Heartbeat: emit desired_state every bar while in a position", group = "Exit Engine",
     tooltip = "Level-triggered in addition to edge-triggered, so a missed MODIFY self-heals within one bar. The server dedupes on idempotency_key.")
emitLifecycle   = input.bool(true, "Emit SCALE / MODIFY / EXIT events (requires patched server)", group = "Exit Engine",
     tooltip = "Lifecycle payloads carry action=MANAGE, which the UNPATCHED TVSignal model rejects (Literal BUY|SELL) — a safe failure, but noisy. Turn OFF until SERVER_PATCH.md item 9 is applied; ENTRY payloads still carry the initial stop.")

var int   posSide        = 0        // 0 flat, 1 long (long-only engine)
var int   posStrat       = 0
var float posEntry       = na
var float posRisk        = na
var float posStop0       = na       // initial stop
var float posStop        = na       // working stop: initial → breakeven → trailed
var float posPartial     = na       // +R partial level (S3/S4), na for S1
var float posExtreme     = na       // highest high since entry
var bool  posPartialDone = false
var bool  posTrailOn     = false
var bool  posPendingBE   = false
var int   posEntryTime   = 0
var int   posEntryBar    = 0
var float posSizePct     = 0.0      // % of original size still open
var int   posEvents      = 0        // lifecycle events emitted for this position


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                       GATES AND FIRE CONDITION                           ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// [F6] Warmup. Regime needs the 50-bar BBW and ATR baselines; the percentiles
// need a real sample. v1 had no gate and emitted confident-looking output from
// bar 1 on freshly listed symbols.
warmupOk = bar_index >= 100 and not na(dAtr) and not na(dSma200) and not na(bbwSMA) and
     not na(rvPctile) and not na(dAtrPct) and nz(dCtxBars) >= math.round(ctxBpy * 0.8)

// [F12] Session gate. Replaces v1's `hour(time_close) == 13`, which was valid
// only for 4H US-equity bars and on a 5m chart fired exactly once a day at 13:00.
inSession = not useSessionGate or not timeframe.isintraday or
     not na(time(timeframe.period, gateSession))
lastBarOk = not fireOnLastBar or not timeframe.isintraday or session.islastbar
hourOk    = noEntryAfter == 0 or not timeframe.isintraday or hour(time_close) < noEntryAfter

// Liquidity from the DAILY context — twenty days on every timeframe.
liquidityOk = (minDollarVol <= 0.0 or (not na(dAdvUsd) and dAdvUsd >= minDollarVol * 1000000.0)) and
     (minPrice <= 0.0 or close >= minPrice)

// [F13] Cooldown in wall-clock minutes, not bars.
var int lastSigTime = 0
cooldownOk = lastSigTime == 0 or (time - lastSigTime) >= effCooldown * 60000

fireSignal = barstate.isconfirmed and warmupOk and bestStrat > 0 and posSide == 0 and
     rrOk and liquidityOk and inSession and lastBarOk and hourOk and cooldownOk


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                     EXIT ENGINE — per-bar update                          ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// Order within a bar mirrors the broker emulator: gap fills at the open, then
// intrabar stop/target with the open→high→low vs open→low→high rule when both
// are inside the range, then the time stop at the close, then close-of-bar
// stop management that takes effect NEXT bar.
evEntry   = false
evPartial = false
evExit    = false
evModify  = false
float evExitPx  = na
evExitWhy = ""
float evFillPx  = na
stopBefore = posStop

if barstate.isconfirmed and posSide == 1 and bar_index > posEntryBar
    stopHit = low  <= posStop
    stopGap = open <= posStop
    tgtAct  = not posPartialDone and not na(posPartial)
    tgtHit  = tgtAct and high >= posPartial
    tgtGap  = tgtAct and open >= posPartial
    whyStop = posStop == posStop0 ? "SL" : posStop == posEntry ? "BE" : "TRAIL"

    if stopGap
        evExit := true
        evExitPx := open
        evExitWhy := whyStop + "_GAP"
    else if tgtGap
        evPartial := true
        evFillPx := open
    else if stopHit and tgtHit
        highFirst = math.abs(high - open) < math.abs(open - low)
        if highFirst
            evPartial := true
            evFillPx := posPartial
            evExit := true
            evExitPx := posStop
            evExitWhy := whyStop      // remainder stopped later in the bar
        else
            evExit := true
            evExitPx := posStop
            evExitWhy := whyStop
    else if stopHit
        evExit := true
        evExitPx := posStop
        evExitWhy := whyStop
    else if tgtHit
        evPartial := true
        evFillPx := posPartial

    if evPartial
        posPartialDone := true
        posSizePct     := posSizePct - exit_partialPct
        posPendingBE   := true
        posTrailOn     := true

    // S1 keeps the profile time stop; S3/S4 do not.
    if not evExit and posStrat == 1 and time - posEntryTime >= p_timeStopDays * 86400000
        evExit := true
        evExitPx := close
        evExitWhy := "TIME"

    if evExit
        posSide := 0
        posSizePct := 0.0
    else
        // close-of-bar management, effective next bar
        if posPendingBE
            posStop      := math.max(posStop, posEntry)
            posPendingBE := false
        posExtreme := math.max(nz(posExtreme, high), high)
        if posTrailOn and not na(atr)
            posStop := math.max(posStop, math.round_to_mintick(posExtreme - exit_trailK * atr))
        evModify := posStop != stopBefore

if fireSignal
    posSide        := 1
    posStrat       := bestStrat
    posEntry       := entryRef
    posRisk        := realRisk
    posStop0       := stopPrice
    posStop        := stopPrice
    posPartial     := bestStrat == 1 ? na : math.round_to_mintick(entryRef + exit_partialR * realRisk)
    posExtreme     := entryRef                // labeller seeds the chandelier extreme at the entry close
    posPartialDone := bestStrat == 1
    posTrailOn     := bestStrat == 1          // S1 trails from entry; S3/S4 after the partial
    posPendingBE   := false
    posEntryTime   := time
    posEntryBar    := bar_index
    posSizePct     := 100.0
    posEvents      := 0
    evEntry        := true

anyEvent  = evEntry or (emitLifecycle and (evPartial or evExit or evModify))
heartbeat = emitHeartbeat and emitLifecycle and barstate.isconfirmed and posSide == 1 and not anyEvent

// Composite score for cross-sectional ranking server-side. S1 wants distance
// FROM the 52-week high (room to revert); the trend strategies want proximity
// TO it. na-guarded so a warmup symbol cannot rank on defaults.
dist52Comp     = bestStrat == 1 ? nz(distFromHi, 50.0) : nz(distFromLo, 50.0)
compositeScore = bestScore * 0.50 + regimeConf * 0.20 + nz(rvPctile, 50.0) * 0.15 +
     (100.0 - nz(dAtrPct, 50.0)) * 0.05 + dist52Comp * 0.10


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                       CONFIDENCE  [F2]                                   ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// The executor sizes on this field and v1 never sent it, so every signal took
// the unset default of 1.5% NAV and the entire scoring engine had no effect on
// capital at risk. Emitting it is the fix. Emitting a SCORE-DERIVED value is a
// separate decision that must wait for Phase 2 — an unvalidated rubric should
// not be choosing position size. Default OFF reproduces today's flat 1.5%.
scoreFloor = bestStrat == 4 ? s4_minScore : 0.0
confRaw = useScoreConfidence ?
     confAtMin + (bestScore - scoreFloor) / math.max(1.0, 100.0 - scoreFloor) * (confAtMax - confAtMin) :
     confFlat
confidence = math.min(0.99, math.max(0.31, confRaw))


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                       WEBHOOK PAYLOAD  [F1]                              ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
secType      = input.string("STK", "sec_type", options = ["STK", "OPT", "FUT"], group = "Webhook",
     tooltip = "The TVSignal model's actual default is STK. v1's header claimed OPT and 'options-only pipeline', which was wrong — exactly the vocabulary drift that header said it was preventing.")
accountRoute = input.string("IBKR_TAXABLE", "account_route",
     options = ["IBKR_TAXABLE", "IBKR_IRA", "FIDELITY_403B_MANUAL"], group = "Webhook")
exchangeHint = input.string("", "exchange hint (blank = SMART)", group = "Webhook")

// The payload is deliberately DUAL-FORM.
//
//   Top-level `stop`, `price`, `comment`, `strategy` are fields the CURRENT
//   TVSignal model already declares, so the stop and the decision context
//   arrive intact even before the server is patched. This is the part that
//   fixes production today.
//
//   The nested blocks below are schema v2 for the patched server. Pydantic's
//   default extra='ignore' means an unpatched server drops them silently
//   rather than 422-ing, so shipping both is safe.
safeTicker = str.replace_all(syminfo.ticker, '"', '\\"')
f2(float v) => str.tostring(v, "0.##")
f1(float v) => str.tostring(v, "0.#")

var int sigSeq = 0
evKind   = evEntry ? "ENTRY" : evExit ? "EXIT" : evPartial ? "SCALE" : evModify ? "MODIFY" : "HEARTBEAT"
signalId = safeTicker + "|" + profileStr + "|" + str.tostring(time) + "|" + evKind + "|" + str.tostring(sigSeq)
// ENTRY is a BUY the current TVSignal model understands. Lifecycle events are
// MANAGE: the unpatched model rejects that literal outright, which is the safe
// failure — a SELL would have opened a short.
payloadAction = evEntry ? "BUY" : "MANAGE"

eventsJson = "[" +
     (evEntry   ? '{"type":"ENTRY","price":' + f2(entryRef) + ',"stop":' + f2(stopPrice) +
                  (bestStrat == 1 ? "" : ',"partial_at":' + f2(posPartial) + ',"partial_pct":' + str.tostring(exit_partialPct)) + '}' : "") +
     (evPartial ? (evEntry ? "," : "") + '{"type":"SCALE","price":' + f2(evFillPx) + ',"pct":' + str.tostring(exit_partialPct) + '}' : "") +
     (evExit    ? ((evEntry or evPartial) ? "," : "") + '{"type":"EXIT","price":' + f2(evExitPx) + ',"reason":"' + evExitWhy + '"}' : "") +
     (evModify and not evExit ? ((evEntry or evPartial) ? "," : "") + '{"type":"MODIFY","stop":' + f2(posStop) + ',"from":' + f2(nz(stopBefore)) + '}' : "") +
     (heartbeat ? '{"type":"HEARTBEAT"}' : "") +
     "]"

dsSide    = posSide == 1 ? "LONG" : "FLAT"
dsStopStr = posSide == 1 ? f2(posStop) : "null"
dsPartStr = posSide == 1 and not na(posPartial) and not posPartialDone ? f2(posPartial) : "null"
dsTrailStr = posSide == 1 and posTrailOn ? f2(nz(posExtreme) - exit_trailK * atr) : "null"
dsTimeStop = posSide == 1 and posStrat == 1 ? str.tostring(posEntryTime + p_timeStopDays * 86400000) : "null"

// Compact digest for the `comment` field — the one free-text channel that
// reaches the executor on an unpatched server.
digest = "ASR2|" + profileStr + "|" + stratTag(bestStrat) +
     "|sc=" + f1(bestScore) + "|cf=" + str.tostring(confidence, "0.00") +
     "|rr=" + f1(rrRatio) + "|sl=" + f2(stopPrice) + "|tp=" + f2(tpPrice) +
     "|rg=" + regimeStr + "|rv=" + f1(nz(rvPctile, 50.0)) + "|cmp=" + f1(compositeScore)


payload =
 '{' +
   '"schema_version":"2.1.0",' +
   '"signal_id":"' + signalId + '",' +
   '"profile":"' + profileStr + '",' +
   '"account_route":"' + accountRoute + '",' +
   '"manual_only":' + (accountRoute == "FIDELITY_403B_MANUAL" ? "true" : "false") + ',' +
   // --- fields the current TVSignal model already accepts ---
   '"symbol":"' + safeTicker + '",' +
   '"action":"' + payloadAction + '",' +
   '"event":"' + evKind + '",' +
   '"events":' + eventsJson + ','
   '"qty":1,' +
   '"order_type":"MKT",' +
   '"price":' + f2(entryRef) + ',' +
   '"stop":' + f2(stopPrice) + ',' +
   '"tif":"DAY",' +
   '"sec_type":"' + secType + '",' +
   '"exchange":"' + exchangeHint + '",' +
   '"strategy":"' + stratName(bestStrat) + '",' +
   '"comment":"' + digest + '",' +
   // --- schema v2 ---
   '"confidence":' + str.tostring(confidence, "0.00") + ',' +
   '"thesis":{' +
     '"direction":"' + (isLong ? "LONG" : "SHORT") + '",' +
     '"horizon_days":' + str.tostring(p_timeStopDays) + ',' +
     '"expected_move_atr":' + f2(atr > 0 ? tpDist / atr : 0.0) +
   '},' +
   '"desired_state":{' +
     '"side":"' + dsSide + '",' +
     '"strategy":"' + stratName(posSide == 1 ? posStrat : bestStrat) + '",' +
     '"entry_ref":' + (posSide == 1 ? f2(posEntry) : f2(entryRef)) + ',' +
     '"risk":' + (posSide == 1 ? f2(posRisk) : f2(realRisk)) + ',' +
     '"stop":' + dsStopStr + ',' +
     '"size_pct_open":' + str.tostring(posSizePct, "0") + ',' +
     '"partial_at":' + dsPartStr + ',' +
     '"partial_pct":' + str.tostring(exit_partialPct) + ',' +
     '"trail":{"type":"CHANDELIER_ATR","k":' + str.tostring(exit_trailK, "0.#") + ',"active":' + (posTrailOn and posSide == 1 ? "true" : "false") + ',"level":' + dsTrailStr + '},' +
     '"breakeven_after_partial":true,' +
     '"time_stop_at":' + dsTimeStop + ',' +
     '"bars_in_trade":' + str.tostring(posSide == 1 ? bar_index - posEntryBar : 0) +
   '},' +
   '"sizing":{' +
     '"stop_distance":' + f2(realRisk) + ',' +
     '"stop_pct":' + f2(stopPct) + ',' +
     '"rr_ratio":' + f2(rrRatio) + ',' +
     '"atr_chart":' + f2(atr) + ',' +
     '"atr_daily":' + f2(nz(dAtr)) +
   '},' +
   '"scores":{' +
     '"conviction":' + f1(bestScore) + ',' +
     '"composite":' + f1(compositeScore) + ',' +
     '"winner":"' + stratTag(bestStrat) + '",' +
     '"s1":' + f1(math.max(s1L, s1S)) + ',' +
     '"s3":' + f1(math.max(s3L, s3S)) + ',' +
     '"s4":' + f1(math.max(s4L, s4S)) + ',' +
     '"calibrated":false' +
   '},' +
   '"regime":{' +
     '"label":"' + regimeStr + '",' +
     '"confidence":' + f1(regimeConf) + ',' +
     '"secondary":"' + regime2Str + '",' +
     '"secondary_score":' + f1(r2Score) + ',' +
     '"trend":' + f1(trendScore) + ',' +
     '"breakout":' + f1(breakoutScore) + ',' +
     '"meanrev":' + f1(meanRevScore) + ',' +
     '"momentum":' + f1(momentumScore) +
   '},' +
   '"context":{' +
     '"feature_basis":"daily",' +
     '"rsi":' + f1(rsi14) + ',' +
     '"adx":' + f1(adxVal) + ',' +
     '"chop":' + f1(nz(chop, 50.0)) + ',' +
     '"atr_pctile":' + f1(nz(dAtrPct, 50.0)) + ',' +
     '"rel_vol_pctile":' + f1(nz(rvPctile, 50.0)) + ',' +
     '"roc_20d":' + f2(nz(dRoc20)) + ',' +
     '"roc_60d":' + f2(nz(dRoc60)) + ',' +
     '"roc_126d":' + f2(nz(dRoc126)) + ',' +
     '"mom_12_1":' + f2(nz(dMom121)) + ',' +
     '"dist_52wk_hi":' + f1(nz(distFromHi, 50.0)) + ',' +
     '"dist_52wk_lo":' + f1(nz(distFromLo, 50.0)) + ',' +
     '"rsi_daily":' + f1(nz(dRsi, 50.0)) + ',' +
     '"adx_daily":' + f1(nz(dAdx)) + ',' +
     '"adv20_usd":' + str.tostring(nz(dAdvUsd), "0") + ',' +
     '"avg_gap_pct":' + f2(nz(dGapAvg)) +
   '},' +
   '"meta":{' +
     '"bar_time":' + str.tostring(time) + ',' +
     '"bar_close_time":' + str.tostring(time_close) + ',' +
     '"tf":"' + timeframe.period + '",' +
     '"warmup_ok":true,' +
     '"bars_per_day":' + f2(bpd) + ',' +
     '"bpd_drift_pct":' + f1(bpdDrift) + ',' +
     '"script_version":"3.0.0"' +
   '}' +
 '}'

if fireSignal
    lastSigTime := time
if anyEvent or heartbeat
    sigSeq += 1
    alert(payload, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                        VISUALIZATION                                     ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// What is drawn is the exit engine's live state — the entry it declared, the
// stop it is working now, and the partial level until it fills. Nothing here
// is broker state; it is the same desired_state the payload carries.
plot(posSide == 1 ? posEntry : na,   "Entry (engine)",        color = color.new(color.white, 30), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(posSide == 1 ? posStop : na,    "Working stop (engine)", color = posTrailOn ? color.new(color.orange, 0) : color.new(color.red, 0), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)
plot(posSide == 1 and not posPartialDone ? posPartial : na, "Partial level (engine)", color = color.new(color.green, 0), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)

plot(dSma200, "SMA200 (daily ctx)", color = color.new(color.gray, 20), linewidth = 1)
plot(s3_fast, "EMA Fast",  color = color.new(color.blue, 40))
plot(s3_slow, "EMA Slow",  color = color.new(color.orange, 40))

plotshape(fireSignal and isLong  and not showStratLabel, "Long",  shape.triangleup,
     location.belowbar, color.green, size = size.small)
plotshape(fireSignal and not isLong and not showStratLabel, "Short", shape.triangledown,
     location.abovebar, color.red, size = size.small)
plotshape(fireSignal and isLong  and showStratLabel, "Long tagged", shape.labelup,
     location.belowbar, color.green, text = "L", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(fireSignal and not isLong and showStratLabel, "Short tagged", shape.labeldown,
     location.abovebar, color.red, text = "S", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

bgcolor(showRegimeBG ? (regime == 4 ? color.new(color.green, 96) : regime == 2 ? color.new(color.yellow, 95) :
     regime == 3 ? color.new(color.blue, 96) : regime == 1 ? color.new(color.purple, 96) :
     color.new(color.gray, 98)) : na, title = "Regime BG")


// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║                            DASHBOARD                                     ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// The BLOCK row is the point of this table: when nothing is firing it names the
// single gate responsible, which is the question you actually have when staring
// at a quiet chart.
blockReason = not warmupOk           ? "WARMUP"      :
     bestStrat == 0                  ? "NO SETUP"    :
     posSide != 0                    ? "IN POSITION" :
     not rrOk                        ? "R:R"         :
     not liquidityOk                 ? "LIQUIDITY"   :
     not inSession                   ? "SESSION"     :
     not lastBarOk                   ? "NOT LAST BAR":
     not hourOk                      ? "TIME CUTOFF" :
     not cooldownOk                  ? "COOLDOWN"    : "READY"

var table tbl = table.new(position.top_right, 4, 15, border_color = color.gray, border_width = 1,
     frame_color = color.gray, frame_width = 2)

if barstate.islast and showDash
    okCol = color.green
    noCol = color.gray

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, syminfo.ticker, bgcolor = color.black, text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 0, timeframe.period, bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 0, profileStr, bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 0, "v2.0 P1", bgcolor = color.black, text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)

    rgCol = regime == 4 ? color.green : regime == 2 ? color.yellow : regime == 3 ? color.blue :
            regime == 1 ? color.purple : color.gray
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 1, "REGIME", bgcolor = color.maroon, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 1, regimeStr, text_color = rgCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 1, str.tostring(regimeConf, "#"), text_color = rgCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 1, "2nd " + regime2Str, text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 2, "S1 MeanRev",  bgcolor = color.new(color.purple, 50), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 2, s1_trigL ? "TRIG" : "—", text_color = s1_trigL ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 2, "trend " + str.tostring(s1_trendC, "#") + "/" + str.tostring(s1_trendGate, "#"), text_color = s1_trendC >= s1_trendGate ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 2, not p_s1Enabled ? "off (profile)" : s1_elig ? "ELIGIBLE" : "—", text_color = s1_elig ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 3, "S3 Momentum", bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 50), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 3, s3_trigL ? "TRIG" : "—", text_color = s3_trigL ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 3, str.tostring(s3_scoreLong, "#") + (p_s3EmitAll ? " (meta)" : "/" + str.tostring(s3_minScoreGate, "#")), text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 3, s3_elig ? "ELIGIBLE" : "—", text_color = s3_elig ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 4, "S4 MTF",      bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 50), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 4, s4_trigL ? "TRIG" : "—", text_color = s4_trigL ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 4, str.tostring(s4_scoreLong, "#") + "/" + str.tostring(s4_minScore, "#"), text_color = s4_scoreLong >= s4_minScore ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 4, s4_elig ? "ELIGIBLE" : "—", text_color = s4_elig ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 5, "Shorts", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 50), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 5, shortEnabled ? "meta only" : "off", text_color = noCol, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 5, shortEnabled ? str.tostring(math.max(s1S, math.max(s3S, s4S)), "#") : "", text_color = noCol, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 5, "never deployed", text_color = noCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 6, "WINNER", bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 6, bestStrat > 0 ? stratTag(bestStrat) + " BUY" : "—", text_color = bestStrat > 0 ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 6, bestStrat > 0 ? "score " + str.tostring(bestScore, "#") : "", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 6, "comp " + str.tostring(compositeScore, "0.#"), text_color = color.yellow, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 7, "BLOCK", bgcolor = color.maroon, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 7, blockReason, text_color = blockReason == "READY" ? okCol : color.orange, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 7, "conf " + str.tostring(confidence, "0.00"),
         text_color = useScoreConfidence ? color.yellow : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 7, useScoreConfidence ? "score-derived" : "flat (unvalidated)",
         text_color = useScoreConfidence ? color.orange : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 8, "Risk", bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 8, (posSide == 1 ? "stop " : "SL ") + str.tostring(posSide == 1 ? posStop : stopPrice, "0.##"),
         text_color = posSide == 1 and posTrailOn ? color.orange : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 8, posSide == 1 ? (posPartialDone ? "partial done" : "partial " + str.tostring(posPartial, "0.##")) :
         (bestStrat == 1 ? "ref TP " + str.tostring(tpPrice, "0.##") : "partial +" + str.tostring(exit_partialR, "0.#") + "R"),
         text_color = color.green, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 8, "R:R " + str.tostring(rrRatio, "0.#") + " / " + str.tostring(effMinRR, "0.#") +
         "  " + str.tostring(stopPct, "0.#") + "%",
         text_color = rrOk ? okCol : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 9, "Daily ctx", bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 9, "ROC20 " + str.tostring(nz(dRoc20), "0.#") + "%", text_color = nz(dRoc20) > 0 ? okCol : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 9, "ROC60 " + str.tostring(nz(dRoc60), "0.#") + "%", text_color = nz(dRoc60) > 0 ? okCol : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 9, "12-1 " + str.tostring(nz(dMom121), "0.#") + "%",  text_color = nz(dMom121) > 0 ? okCol : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 10, "Percentiles", bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 10, "ATR " + str.tostring(nz(dAtrPct, 50.0), "#") + "p", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 10, "rVol " + str.tostring(nz(rvPctile, 50.0), "#") + "p", text_color = nz(rvPctile, 50.0) > 70 ? okCol : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 10, "52wk lo " + str.tostring(nz(distFromLo, 50.0), "#") + "%", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 11, "Liquidity", bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 11, "$" + str.tostring(nz(dAdvUsd) / 1000000.0, "0.#") + "M", text_color = liquidityOk ? okCol : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 11, "20-day ADV", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 11, "gap " + str.tostring(nz(dGapAvg), "0.##") + "%", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 12, "TF norm", bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 12, "bpd " + str.tostring(bpd, "0.##"), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 12, timeframe.isintraday and sessSeen >= 5 ? "obs " + str.tostring(bpdObs, "0.#") : "ctx " + str.tostring(ctxBpy),
         text_color = bpdDrift > 20.0 ? color.red : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 12, bpdDrift > 20.0 ? "CHECK sessionSec" : "ok", text_color = bpdDrift > 20.0 ? color.red : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 13, "Cooldown", bgcolor = color.navy, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 13, cooldownOk ? "READY" : str.tostring(int(math.ceil((effCooldown * 60000 - (time - lastSigTime)) / 60000.0))) + "m",
         text_color = cooldownOk ? okCol : color.orange, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 13, "of " + str.tostring(effCooldown) + "m", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 13, "signals " + str.tostring(sigSeq), text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 14, "Position", bgcolor = color.black, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 14, posSide == 1 ? "LONG " + stratTag(posStrat) + " " + str.tostring(posSizePct, "0") + "%" : "FLAT",
         text_color = posSide == 1 ? okCol : noCol, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 2, 14, posSide == 1 ? "@ " + str.tostring(posEntry, "0.##") + "  " + str.tostring(bar_index - posEntryBar) + "b" : "",
         text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 3, 14, posSide == 1 ? (posTrailOn ? "trailing" : "initial stop") + " (engine, not broker)" : "",
         text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
